WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.189
Ukrainian forces are accelerating

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:03.599
their territorial advances

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.309
into Russian-held areas.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:08.819
Vladimir Putin's military could be

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.139
on the verge of collapse.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:12.359
Russian President Vladimir Putin now

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.639
threatening to use nuclear

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:15.599
weapons.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.219
Biden said the risk of nuclear

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.469
Armageddon is at the highest level

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.479
since 1962.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:22.799
President Biden has said that the

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.119
world hasn't been this close to

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.459
nuclear Armageddon since the 1962

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.109
Cuban Missile Crisis.

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:29.639
Vladimir Putin has issued grave

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.649
threats and then backtracked.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:33.209
In late September, he announced in a

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:34.799
televised address that he would use

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.299
all available means to protect

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.709
Russia and our people.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:39.929
"This is not a bluff", he said.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.849
Then in a speech on October 27th,

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.079
he said, referring to nuclear

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.759
weapons, "There is no point in that,

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.739
neither political nor military."

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.449
But The New York Times reported last

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:49.979
week that Russian military leaders

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.749
recently held meetings without Putin

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:53.429
to discuss when and how to use

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:55.799
tactical nuclear weapons in Ukraine.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.989
Antiwar.com's Scott Horton, editor

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:59.669
of the new book Hotter than the Sun

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:01.679
Time to Abolish Nuclear Weapons.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.299
Says that we should take seriously

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.829
the idea that the conflict in

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.059
Ukraine could escalate to

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.739
a world-ending war.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.629
From the very beginning of the war.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.159
I mean, in his declaration of war,

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:12.479
he threatened to use nukes against

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.369
any country that intervened, namely

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:16.559
us. And then his defense minister

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:17.999
and head of its National Security

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.680
Council as former President Medvedev

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:23.309
is Foreign Minister Lavrov

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:24.239
as well. They've all threatened to

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:26.459
use nuclear weapons since this war

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:28.199
began at different times.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.689
Biden's stated policy

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.309
is to help Ukraine no matter how

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:33.539
long it takes to win back their

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:34.679
territory.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.899
That logically can't be accomplished

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:37.889
without throwing us in

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:39.989
extraordinarily high nuclear

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:40.499
risk.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.239
Daniel Davis, a senior fellow for

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:43.709
defense priorities and a former

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:44.999
lieutenant colonel in the U.S.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.949
Army, believes that despite recent

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:48.449
setbacks, the Russian army is

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:50.699
unlikely to back down any time soon.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:52.799
I don't buy into the narrative

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.659
that the Russian army writ large is

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:56.999
trash, and I hear that all the time,

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.439
or that they've been humiliated.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:01:59.549
They have made a number of

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:00.899
significant mistakes, but they've

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.369
also shown that they can learn from

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:03.749
mistakes. And some time in the

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:05.189
latter part of November and first

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:06.839
part of December, there is an

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:08.099
expected massive

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.100
invasion re-invasion

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:11.008
re-offensive coming.

00:02:11.009 --> 00:02:11.849
I think you're going to see a

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:13.349
significant swing back in the

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:14.579
Russian side at that point.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.199
Ukrainian President Vladimir

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.909
Zelensky said in late October that

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:19.499
his goal was to drive Russia out of

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.119
all parts of Ukraine, including

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:23.639
Crimea, which it annexed in 2014.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.589
The Russian military would fight

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:26.639
to the T to keep that from

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:28.379
happening, but in the event that the

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:30.329
policy was successful, then

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.369
the chance goes way up

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:34.379
that Russia would use

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.969
nuclear weapons. Because I don't

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:38.009
think that Putin can survive

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:40.049
if he allowed his troops his merely

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:41.699
his conventional forces to be

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.679
defeated and physically driven

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.779
back into Russia and not used

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:46.979
nuclear weapons. I don't think the

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:48.659
hardliners in his country would

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.339
allow him to stay in power if he did

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:51.929
it. And I think he knows that what

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:53.909
we should be doing is, hey, let's

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:55.889
let's help Ukraine with

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:57.539
defensive weapons so that they keep

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:58.919
Russia from just rolled it across

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:01.499
them. At the same time, backdoor

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:03.479
negotiations and diplomatic

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:05.159
channels with both sides to say,

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.629
hey, y'all figure this out.

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:07.889
Figure out a way that we can bring

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:10.169
this to an end for everybody's

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:12.119
sake. But we should not be

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.189
pursuing something that probably

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:15.209
can't be accomplished.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:17.039
And if it did, it would put us in

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:18.189
nuclear risk.

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:19.529
Horton says that a diplomatic

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:20.729
solution could have been reached

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:22.079
back in April, pointing to an

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:24.089
article co-written by Fiona Hill,

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:25.529
a former senior director for

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:27.089
European and Russian affairs on the

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:29.099
National Security Council, stating

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.569
that, according to multiple former

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:32.919
senior U.S. officials in April

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:34.649
2022, Russian and Ukrainian

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:35.999
negotiators appeared to have

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.769
tentatively agreed on the outlines

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:39.659
of a negotiated interim settlement.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.429
According to a Ukrainian newspaper

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:42.689
and a press release from the British

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:44.219
government, then prime minister

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:45.989
Boris Johnson urged Zelensky to

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:48.149
avoid such negotiations with Russia.

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:50.099
They had a deal in principle

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.989
ready to be signed where the

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:54.239
Russians would end the war,

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:55.829
agree to pull back to where they

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.749
were on February the 23rd.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:58.919
So that's like, you know, just

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.629
barely into the Donbass region in

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:01.889
the very early hours of the

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:03.149
invasion, essentially.

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:04.919
And and then that would be it.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.599
They would call a truce right there.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:08.339
But Ukraine would have to, you know,

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:09.329
I guess, enshrine it in their

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:11.249
constitution and give a real

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.259
guarantee that they would forswear

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:15.359
any future attempt to join

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:17.429
the NATO alliance and then

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:18.898
essentially force, you know,

00:04:18.899 --> 00:04:20.398
guarantee their neutrality going

00:04:20.399 --> 00:04:21.479
forward. And that would have been

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:21.719
it.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.339
In late September, Putin announced

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:24.959
the annexation of four Ukrainian

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:26.729
territories that border Russia,

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:27.989
asserting that residents of the

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:29.339
occupied territories would be

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:31.169
Russian citizens forever.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.639
The Kremlin warned that Ukrainian

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:34.259
attacks against any of the annexed

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:35.489
regions would be considered

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:37.529
aggression against Russia itself.

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:39.059
Now you're asking me.

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:41.129
In early October,

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:43.469
after Putin has made this

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.539
terrible escalation

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:47.429
in semantics

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.979
only, but it means everything.

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:51.869
He has now claimed to

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:54.749
have absorbed what

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:55.949
I don't know how many square miles.

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:57.869
These four huge oblast,

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:00.279
these provinces of Eastern Ukraine

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:02.019
here to get him to back down from

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:03.909
that. I think it's going

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:06.129
to be virtually impossible now.

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:07.689
I would tell Blinken, I would, like,

00:05:07.690 --> 00:05:09.669
grab him by his ear like his angry

00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:10.599
step mom.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:12.279
Right. And help him get on the

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:14.229
plane. Go to Geneva,

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:16.329
tell Lavrov you're sorry

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:17.829
and you're willing to try to work

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:19.488
this out now and find a way,

00:05:19.489 --> 00:05:21.939
dammit. Ceasefire first

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:24.039
and then see what we can do.

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:25.869
Nobody in Ukraine and nobody in

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:27.819
the West wants to allow Russia

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:29.799
to keep one inch of territory

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:30.849
that they've taken.

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:33.009
But look, I'm just going to be blunt

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:34.989
and just say this straight up.

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:37.029
We have to deal with the reality

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:39.069
that exists, not the picture

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:40.539
that we wish existed.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:42.399
The picture we wish existed is

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:44.109
that we'll just give Ukraine enough

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.089
support and eventually they'll drag

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:47.139
Russia back and they'll have all

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:49.029
their territory and then

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:50.299
there'll be a full hold in

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:51.219
democratic country.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:52.509
I mean, that's what we say and

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:54.189
that's what we would desire.

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:56.319
But we have to bank on reality,

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:58.479
because the truth is that the harsh

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:00.459
core, hard core reality

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.139
is that to try and accomplish that

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:04.179
objective is to almost certainly

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:06.039
escalate the fight to

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:07.359
a nuclear conflict.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:09.189
So we instead have to do what is

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:10.989
realistically possible.

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:12.789
And what is realistically possible

00:06:12.790 --> 00:06:14.919
is to freeze the war where it's at

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:16.889
right now before Ukraine loses

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:18.399
any more territory.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:20.829
And while they have a chance

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:23.109
to make some kind of negotiation

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:24.969
to where they can keep the majority

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:26.829
of their country and then

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:28.959
have some kind of cessation

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:30.279
of war, that where they can at least

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:32.169
live next door to each other.

00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:33.369
And then there's no more threat of a

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:35.259
war for anyone. No more refugees,

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:36.969
no more cities destroyed, no more

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:38.559
people killed, no more soldiers

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:40.299
lost. That's what we should be

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:41.019
shooting for.

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:42.909
Yale historian Timothy Snyder has

00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:44.469
written that negotiating with Putin

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:46.329
will only make future nuclear war

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:48.219
much more likely because the lesson

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:49.839
for future dictators would be that

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:51.519
all they need is a nuclear weapon

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:52.899
and some bluster to get what they

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:53.469
want.

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:54.879
Nothing's changed because of this

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:56.439
conflict. I mean, that already

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:58.479
exists, and that's part

00:06:58.480 --> 00:06:59.289
of the reality.

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:01.209
Russia has nuclear weapons.

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:03.369
North Korea has nuclear weapons.

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:04.989
You're not going to roll that back.

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:06.159
So we need to keep that number

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:08.199
small, but we also

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:09.729
have to concurrently deal.

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:11.109
And I keep saying this with the

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:12.129
reality.

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:13.719
Reality is Russia has nuclear

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:15.609
weapons and it can escalate.

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:17.439
So we have to deal where we can.

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:19.809
Now, let me also add in to that,

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:22.509
that it's a myth to suggest

00:07:22.510 --> 00:07:24.309
that, oh, well, look, Russia all

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:25.869
they did is have to have nuclear

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:27.789
threats. And, you know, now then

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:29.109
they get all this stuff.

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:31.479
Look, Russia has so badly

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:33.219
harmed itself with all of the losses

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:34.869
that it sustained up to this point

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:36.879
already, that it's going to take

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:38.799
decades to recover from that.

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:40.059
A lot of these sanctions will never

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:41.709
be rolled back, at least not in our

00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:42.669
lifetimes.

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:45.399
And so the harm that the nation

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:47.349
of Russia has suffered already

00:07:47.350 --> 00:07:48.729
and will continue to suffer is

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:50.559
significant and hardly a

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:52.059
blueprint for anyone else to want to

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:53.109
follow.

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:54.579
Horton says the war in Ukraine shows

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:56.049
that deterrence is too risky of a

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:57.879
strategy and should reinvigorate the

00:07:57.880 --> 00:07:59.139
push for disarmament.

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:01.119
That only works until it stops

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:03.219
working. And once it stops working,

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:04.409
then that's it.

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:05.409
You know, it's called the Doomsday

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:08.529
Machine because it's made to be used

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:09.549
completely.

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:11.109
I was on Fox News the other night

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:13.239
and the liberal Democrat says, oh,

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:15.039
come on, we have mutually assured

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:15.819
destruction.

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:17.799
In other words, they can't touch

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:20.019
us, so we can do whatever

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:21.939
we want to them in Ukraine

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:22.989
because there's no way they're going

00:08:22.990 --> 00:08:24.039
to reach out and touch us here in

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:25.599
North America because that would be

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:27.249
nuclear war and they would never

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:28.719
dare to do such a thing.

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:29.979
Well, that's just not true.

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:31.479
That kind of thinking is the kind of

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:32.859
thing that'll get us killed.

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:33.939
That's the kind of thinking that

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:35.829
Russia's nuclear arsenal is supposed

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:36.999
to prevent.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:38.739
And yet somehow it doesn't.

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:40.749
There's too much casual talk about,

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:43.479
all of a sudden, American forces

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:45.729
fighting in the war against Russia

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:47.109
on the side of Ukraine.

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:48.909
That is ludicrous.

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:50.739
There is nothing going on

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:52.899
in the border dispute between

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:54.339
Russia and Ukraine that has anything

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:55.569
to do with American national

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:56.559
security.

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:58.539
So the idea that we would risk our

00:08:58.540 --> 00:09:00.819
security by involving ourselves

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:02.889
in this potential war that could

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:04.779
escalate up to a nuclear conflict is

00:09:04.780 --> 00:09:06.939
absurd in the highest degree,

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:08.769
and we should not do it.

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:10.749
I am afraid, John, that it's going

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:12.669
to come down to some

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:14.649
absolutely horrible

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:16.659
incident and somehow hopefully

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:18.609
we get through that and people

00:09:18.610 --> 00:09:20.019
will recognize we've got to scale

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:21.129
back the other way.

00:09:21.130 --> 00:09:22.239
I'm not recommending that.

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:23.319
I'm just saying I don't know what

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:24.549
else is going to get through to

00:09:24.550 --> 00:09:26.379
people. I'm afraid that that's what

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:27.159
it's going to come to.

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:29.289
And frankly, I don't believe that

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:31.209
if one atom bomb goes off,

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:33.399
I don't think that it can stop.

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:35.649
I am on the most pessimistic

00:09:35.650 --> 00:09:36.999
person in the world as far as that

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:38.769
goes. I think if anybody uses an

00:09:38.770 --> 00:09:40.689
atom bomb anywhere, America blows up

00:09:40.690 --> 00:09:41.949
the whole world, period.

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:43.779
Henry Kissinger himself a

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:45.789
few months ago said, "Hey, hey,

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:47.619
we need to find an

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:49.539
exit ramp out of this thing now

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:51.279
before this gets out of control."

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:53.559
That should be all you need to know

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:55.029
about how dangerous this is.

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:56.889
And frankly, I wouldn't mind, he

00:09:56.890 --> 00:09:58.689
would need a chaperon, but I

00:09:58.690 --> 00:09:59.979
wouldn't mind involving him in

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:01.689
diplomacy right now.

00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:03.669
If we sent Henry Kissinger to meet

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:05.979
with Sergei Lavrov in

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:07.809
in Geneva tomorrow, I

00:10:07.810 --> 00:10:09.399
would celebrate that as the greatest

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:10.989
invention of peace in our time right

00:10:10.990 --> 00:10:11.990
now.

